Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HardwareMetal::draw_placed runs a draw end to end the way the app's
raster drives hardware.rs: the uniforms and tables staged through the
ring's stage_block, the placed vertices' 24-float rows staged and the
triangles drawn indexed from the ring, the textures bound by slot,
the render pass with the colour and the depth+stencil twin, commit
and the GPU-side wait. the pipeline builds per key (the DYNAMIC=1
generic — the fragment's spec words baked through prepare, the
bindings the fragment's own per-entry map).

the_draw_executor_runs_placed_vertices: the two halves' pixels come
out the vertices' own colours through this whole path — the app's
draw route proven on the rack's real shaders.

145 tests green.
